# CertGen Core

Serverless Astro app: survey → PDF certificate. Stack: Astro 6 SSR · React 19 · Tailwind 4 · Supabase · Satori · Resvg · PDFKit · Vercel Node.

## Layering

```
pages/api/generate-cert.ts → certificateWorkflow.service.ts
  ├── repositories/* (only layer that talks to Supabase)
  ├── cert-generator.tsx (Satori → PNG)
  └── pdf.service.ts (JPG + PNG → PDF)
```

- API routes validate and delegate — business logic lives in `src/services/`.
- Never call Supabase from React components or Astro pages.
- Keep `@resvg/resvg-js` as a Vite SSR external in `astro.config.mjs`.

## Env vars

Use `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` (not `SUPABASE_KEY`).

## Code style

- TypeScript strict; minimal diffs; no drive-by refactors.
- Prefer code over stale README when docs conflict (output is PDF, templates in `public/templates/`, font is `GoogleSans-Bold.ttf`).

